sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant P as payment-service
    participant T as Durable transport / outbox
    participant W as partner-webhook-service
    participant D as Delivery state
    participant H as Enabled partner endpoint
    participant O as Operations / observability

    P->>T: Publish accepted transition with event_id
    Note over P,T: event_id identifies the accepted transition; it is created once.
    T->>W: Deliver event (at-least-once)
    W->>D: Create or load (partner_id, event_id)
    alt New delivery intent
        W->>H: POST webhook + event_id + X-Payment-Event-Id
        H-->>W: Accepted or classified failure
        W->>D: Record attempt, status, redacted outcome
    else Duplicate delivery message
        W->>D: Suppress duplicate intent; preserve event_id
    end
    W-->>O: State, latency, attempts, and redacted metrics
    alt Transient failure and retry budget remains
        W->>T: Schedule bounded backoff with jitter
        T->>W: Retry same event_id
        W->>H: Retry webhook with same event_id/header
    else Permanent failure or retry budget exhausted
        W->>D: Mark dead-lettered
        W-->>O: DLQ visibility and alert
    end
    O->>W: Authorized, audited replay request
    W->>H: Replay same event_id/header
    W->>D: Record replay attempt and outcome
    Note over W,H: Any migration/coexistence path must share the same identity boundary.
